### D. Federal grant-funded state and local procurement

An important bridge between federal and local jurisdictions is:

2 CFR § 200.318(c)(1) — General procurement standards.

Nonfederal entities conducting procurement transactions under federal awards must maintain written standards of conduct addressing real or apparent conflicts of interest.

The standards must address employee, officer, agent, immediate-family, partner, and organization interests in circumstances specified by the regulation.

This is especially important when a county, municipality, or state agency administers a federally funded homeland security project.

The federal grant relationship does not erase state or local law; multiple requirements may apply simultaneously.

