### B. Illinois

Illinois — Statutory revolving-door restrictions

Illinois has an especially explicit procurement-related revolving-door provision.

The principal authority is:

5 ILCS 430/5-45 — Procurement; revolving door prohibition.

Under subsection (a), a covered former state officer, member, or employee generally cannot, for one year after leaving state service, knowingly accept employment or compensation from an entity when the individual personally and substantially participated in specified state contract awards, fiscal administration, or change orders involving cumulative contract value of $25,000 or more during the preceding year.

The provision also addresses certain spouses and immediate family members living with the covered individual. Other subsections establish additional restrictions for specified senior personnel and circumstances. Illinois General Assembly +2

