Separation-of-authority principle

An agency ethics officer may advise on a conflict without having authority to prosecute a criminal offense. An inspector general may investigate without possessing final adjudicatory authority. A procurement officer may suspend an award without determining criminal liability.

The research should never collapse these separate functions into one institutional finding.

